00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.140
Help me!

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.190
Summer came to Mattis' Forest.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.170
Ronja and Birk finally managed to tame their horses,

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.750
and seem to have grown accustomed to life in the Bear's Cave.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:58.510
Then one day, they returned home to find an unexpected visitor waiting for them.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.420
The Roaring Waterfall and the Wild Harpies

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.420
The Roaring Waterfall and the Wild Harpies

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.740
Lil-Klippen!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.400
Whoa!

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.940
It's really you, right?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.580
You're really here!

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.610
There we go.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.550
This place has got quite the view!

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.750
You can see the river and the woods, can't you?

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.620
Yeah, we sure can.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.730
Did you come here just compliment our place?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:53.020
No, Lovis sent me to give this to you.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.020
Birk! Look at this!

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.600
Bread!

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.640
We've got bread!

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.740
Bread from Lovis!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:10.450
I'd forgotten there was anything so wonderful.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.970
Birk, have some—

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:38.800
Lovis figured you guys would be out of bread just about now.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:46.190
But how did she know I'd be at the Bear's Cave?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.730
Do you think your mother's stupid?

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.960
Where else would you be?

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.070
Look, Ronja...

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.860
Won't you come back home already?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.580
How are thing in Mattis' fort nowadays?

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.210
It's melancholy in Mattis' fort nowadays.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.980
Come back to us, Ronja.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:03.400
Did Lovis send you to say that?

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.800
Yeah...

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.830
It sucks without you there.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:16.080
Ronja, everyone is waiting for you to come back.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.460
Even Mattis?

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.260
Eh?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.930
Is he waiting for me to come back too?

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:41.980
Oh man!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.280
I have no idea what's going on in that guy's head!

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:54.290
Does he even talk about me?

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.700
Well?! Tell me the truth!

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.800
Has he ever mentioned my name, even once?!

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.240
Well, yes... but...

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:20.170
We're not supposed to utter your name within earshot of him.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:33.000
But everything will be all right,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.340
just as long as you come home!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.700
I'm never coming home!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.670
Not as long as I'm not Mattis' child!

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.300
You can tell him that!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.300
In fact, shout it at the top of your lungs!

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.510
I'd sure like to do that...

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:08.860
Not even old Per would dare come out with a message like that.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:27.380
After that was settled, Lil-Klippen told Ronja all about events in Mattis' fort.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.820
The old geezer?

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.160
Per isn't doing so well these days.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:49.070
I dare you guys to say that again!

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:04.130
But with things the way they are, it's not surprising he was having a hard time.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:11.200
And the robbery business has been going badly too.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:17.610
The whole forest is teaming with soldiers.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:23.660
They caught Pelje and put him in one of the Sheriff's dungeons,

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:29.560
where he languished on a diet of bread and water.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:06.320
I heard they put two of Borka's robbers in with him too.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:15.600
The Sheriff has sworn that he'll soon capture all of the robbers in Mattis' wood,

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:19.240
and make them pay for their crimes

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:25.640
I wonder what that would mean for us.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.400
Death, perhaps?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.410
Doesn't he ever laugh these days?

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:40.040
Who? The Sheriff?

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.770
I'm talking about Mattis.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.420
No... He doesn't.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:59.230
No one has heard him laugh since the day you jumped over Hell's Gap.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:10.300
Ronja, come home!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.380
Please?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.040
It's the right thing to do.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.090
If you don't, your mother will...

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:22.180
Say hello to Lovis for me.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.000
Tell her that we're really grateful for the bread.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.130
I forgot, there's salt in there for you too.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.620
Thank you, Lil-Klippen.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.830
Well, well...

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:07.130
So, you didn't go back home to your father with that loser of a robber.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.780
I don't have a father!

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:26.310
And if you don't watch it, I might not have a brother anymore either!

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.760
Forgive me, my sister.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.950
If I'm wrong, that is.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:47.680
But I sometimes know what you're thinking when your mind wanders.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:53.510
Yes, I'm thinking that I've lived for eleven winters,

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:58.200
but the twelfth might be the death of me.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.730
But I want to live, <i>here</i>.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.820
If you can understand that.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.020
Forget about winter.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.550
It's summer now.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:22.750
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:22.750
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:27.090
And indeed, it was summer.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.710
More and more summer everyday.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:40.170
Clearer and warmer than any summer they could remember.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:07.720
Here goes.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.580
Got it.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:27.700
Wow!

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:42.610
Hey, Birk, it's summer all around us!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:52.130
Yeah, but the fun will end quickly if we float too close to Greedy Falls.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:11.650
Yeah, as soon as I catch sight of Greedy Hump, I know it's getting dangerous.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.690
Here it comes!

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:46.220
I'm glad we were able to make it back.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:56.990
Yeah, I'll make it back every single time.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:41.090
These warm summer evenings are lovely for riding.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:12.170
Why can't it always be summer in the forest?

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:19.480
Why does winter have to come?

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:25.350
What's on your mind, sister?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.920
I was thinking about...

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:35.130
Oh yeah! I was wondering whether or not murktrolls live under that huge rock!

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.460
See it? Beyond those trees!

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:44.640
I saw them dancing on top of it when I came to live with you.

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:49.670
I like the murktrolls and rumphobs,

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.410
but not the gray dwarves and wild harpies.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.310
I can't help it.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:02.040
Yeah, who does?

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:15.080
It's getting darker a lot faster then before.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:24.250
It's written all over the stars, "Autumn is coming."

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:25.700
Ronja!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:45.690
Yeah, I hate the wild harpies the most.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:52.580
The wild harpies have left us in peace up here for this long because they don't know about this place.{We only have a nice and peaceful time up here because the Wild Harpies don't know about this place.}{It really is extraordinary that they've left us in peace up here for this long.}

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:59.710
Perhaps the gray dwarves have kept quiet for once.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:05.190
Otherwise we'd have had the harpies swooping down on us long ago.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.090
Let's stop talking about them.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:13.020
It's not good to talk about them.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.330
We might bring them here.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:23.290
Lovely little humans in the water!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.420
Now there will be clawing!

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.800
Now the blood will run!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.050
Dive, Ronja!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:50.720
Where's that precious black-haired human?

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:57.140
Where's that pretty little red-haired human?

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:00.580
Come on out!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.100
Birk!

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:09.930
Birk?!

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.810
Where are you?

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.460
Birk!

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.620
I found you!

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:21.100
Pretty little black-haired human!

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:51.370
We need not to hurry ourselves.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:57.950
Let's make them cower in fear before we claw them to bits.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:05.140
Let them grow even more frantic in anticipation of being town apart.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.330
Ronja! Hurry, come here!

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:09.650
Birk?

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:14.650
Birk?!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.150
Where are you?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.740
I'm here!

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.550
Come on!

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:23.680
Birk!

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:28.160
Where's that pretty red-haired human?

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:51.350
Where's that pretty black haired human?

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:56.720
Where's that pretty red-haired human?

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:59.360
Oh, Birk! I thought you drowned!

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:01.330
Not yet.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.740
But soon.

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:13.180
Where have those lovely little humans gone?

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:16.030
We shall make you bleed!

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:41.320
My sister.

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:44.300
My brother.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:47.900
As long as you are with someone you truly love,

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:52.220
no matter how hard things get, there is nothing to fear.

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:55.340
Such a wonderful thing that is.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:01.270
They had no need for words to
 communicate this to each other.

